---
description: |
  Assembles parsed Linux Audit records into audit events.

  The kernel describes one audited system call with several records, such as
  `SYSCALL`, `EXECVE`, `CWD`, `PATH`, and `PROCTITLE`, that share the stamp
  `msg=audit(<time>:<serial>)`. The operator expects the output of
  `auditd::parse` and replaces each group of records with one event:

  ```tql
  auditd::parse line, record
  auditd::assemble line, record
  ```

  The event holds `node`, `time`, and `serial`, the records
  under `records`, and the original lines in `raw_data`. Records group by node,
  time, and serial. Userspace and daemon records, such as `USER_LOGIN` or
  `DAEMON_START`, form events of their own. The end-of-event marker `EOE`
  carries no data and is not kept.

  Records wait in bounded event-time windows: an event completes once
  the newest record seen is 30 seconds past its window, or after 10 seconds
  without input. Records that arrive later than that, for example from files
  read out of time order, are dropped with a warning. Read rotated files from
  the oldest to the newest.

  Call it between `auditd::parse` and `auditd::ocsf::map` in a staged
  pipeline. `auditd::ocsf::normalize` does this implicitly. Leave it out for
  one OCSF event per record.
args:
  positional:
    - name: line
      type: field
      description: The field holding the `audit.log` line.
    - name: record
      type: field
      description: The parsed record to replace with the assembled event.
---

if $record == null {
  // Lines that are not Linux Audit records pass through.
} else {
  // Kernel records of one event share their stamp. Userspace programs and the
  // audit daemon submit every record on its own, and daemon records can reuse
  // serial zero, so their own line keeps them apart. All records pass the
  // same window, so that userspace and kernel records leave it in the same
  // event-time order.
  $record._own = $line if $record.type.match_regex(r"^(?:USER|CRED_|ACCT_|ADD_|DEL_|GRP_MGMT|ROLE_|SERVICE_|SYSTEM_|DAEMON_|SOFTWARE_UPDATE|TRUSTED_APP|CRYPTO_|USYS_|LABEL_|AVC_PATH_INVALID)") else null
  window size=5s, on=$record.time, tolerance=30s, idle_timeout=10s {
    summarize \
      _node=$record.node,
      _time=$record.time,
      _serial=$record.serial,
      _own=$record._own,
      _records=collect(drop_null_fields({type: $record.type, fields: $record.fields, enriched: $record.enriched})),
      _lines=collect($line)
  }
  batch timeout=1s
  $record = {
    node: _node,
    time: _time,
    serial: _serial,
    records: _records.where(r => r.type != "EOE"),
    raw_data: _lines.join("\n"),
  }
  drop _node, _time, _serial, _own, _records, _lines
  where $record.records.length() > 0
}
